5 - Files
    -----

    A002_00_Premises.v

      Stdlib and A001 import hub for A002. Defines arithmetic result
      conventions, `accept`, `reject`, error stages, error details, and the
      public verifier/checker type aliases.

    A002_01__A001_Wrappers.v

      Canonical A001 destructuring layer. Defines `fst001`, `snd001`,
      `recode001`, `canonical001b`, and `is_pair001b`, then proves the basic
      projection and canonicity facts for freshly encoded A001 pairs.

    A002_02__Tagged_Lists.v

      A001-coded finite list layer. Defines `code_nil`, `code_cons`,
      `code_derivation`, bounded indexing by `nth_list_fuel`, and exact claimed
      length checking by `list_exact_lengthb`.

    A002_03__Formula_Syntax.v

      Formula syntax for the implicational object language. Defines variables,
      implications, bounded formula recognition by `is_formula_fuel`, the total
      wrapper `is_formula`, and the arithmetic implication parser `parse_imp`.

    A002_04__Line_Syntax.v

      Proof-line and rule-tag syntax. Defines `code_line`, `tag_axk`,
      `tag_axs`, `tag_mp`, `parse_rule_tag`, and `parse_line`.

    A002_05__Rule_Checkers_Hilbert.v

      Executable local checkers for the fixed Hilbert core. Implements
      `check_axk`, `check_axs`, and `check_mp`, together with result
      projections and line-formula access helpers.

    A002_06__Verifier_Core.v

      Main bounded verifier. Implements `verify_line`, `verify_lines`,
      `final_formula_result`, and `A002_Verify`. The loop is structurally
      recursive on explicit fuel derived from the claimed derivation length.

    A002_07__Certificates.v

      Certificate naming and checking layer. Defines local and global
      certificate constructors/projections and the executable certificate
      checker `A002_Certb`.

    A002_08__Soundness.v

      Initial theorem surface. Proves verifier acceptance implies
      `A002_Certb`, generated certificates check, deterministic verifier
      behavior, and accepted-result shape facts for the local checkers.

    A002_94_IO.v

      Extraction-facing IO dispatcher. Defines `A002_IO_Query`,
      `A002_IO_Result`, `A002_IO`, parser/verifier diagnostics, and compact
      `*_Z` views using binary integers.

    A002_95_API.v

      Stable public import surface. Re-exports the IO and theorem surface
      through a single package interface.

    A002_97_Artifacts.v

      Artifact layer. Redirects `Print Assumptions` for the public theorem
      names and extracts `A002_Verifier` and `A002_IO` OCaml artifacts.

    _appendix/_artifacts/

      Intended location for extracted OCaml artifacts:
      `A002_Verifier.{ml,mli}` and `A002_IO.{ml,mli}`.

    _appendix/_assumptions/

      Intended location for redirected assumption reports for the public A002
      theorem surface.

    _appendix/examples/

      Intended location for computed examples and failure diagnostics.


6 - API
    ---

    The public theorem and executable surface is exposed by

      `From A002 Require Import A002_95_API.`

    Arithmetic verifier:

      A002_Verify      : nat -> nat -> nat
      A002_Certb       : nat -> nat -> nat -> bool

    A001 canonical destructuring:

      fst001           : nat -> nat
      snd001           : nat -> nat
      recode001        : nat -> nat
      canonical001b    : nat -> bool
      is_pair001b      : nat -> nat -> nat -> bool

    Formula constructors and parsers:

      code_var         : nat -> nat
      code_imp         : nat -> nat -> nat
      is_formula_fuel  : nat -> nat -> bool
      formula_bound    : nat -> nat
      is_formula       : nat -> bool
      parse_imp        : nat -> nat

    List and derivation constructors:

      code_nil         : nat
      code_cons        : nat -> nat -> nat
      code_derivation  : nat -> nat -> nat
      list_exact_lengthb : nat -> nat -> bool
      nth_list_fuel    : nat -> nat -> nat -> nat

    Line and rule constructors:

      code_line        : nat -> nat -> nat
      tag_axk          : nat
      tag_axs          : nat
      tag_mp           : nat -> nat -> nat
      parse_rule_tag   : nat -> nat
      parse_line       : nat -> nat

    Rule checkers:

      check_axk        : nat -> nat
      check_axs        : nat -> nat
      check_mp         : nat -> nat -> nat -> nat -> nat -> nat

    Main theorem surface:

      A002_Verify_accept_sound :
        forall d theta p,
          A002_Verify d theta = encode 1 p ->
          A002_Certb d theta p = true

      A002_generated_cert_checks :
        forall d theta p,
          A002_Verify d theta = encode 1 p ->
          A002_Certb d theta p = true

      A002_Verify_deterministic_export :
        forall d theta r1 r2,
          A002_Verify d theta = r1 ->
          A002_Verify d theta = r2 ->
          r1 = r2

    IO:

      A002_IO          : A002_IO_Query -> A002_IO_Result
      A002_IO_Z        : A002_IO_Query -> A002_IO_Result_Z


7 - Notes
    -----

    A002 intentionally depends on A001 for all pairing and unpairing. It does
    not redefine `encode` or `decode`. The verifier returns natural numbers
    only. A successful result is decoded as

      encode 1 p

    and a failed result is decoded as

      encode 0 (encode stage (encode index detail)).

    The current `A002_Certb` is an executable generated-certificate checker:
    it reruns `A002_Verify d theta` and compares the result with `accept p`.
    This is arithmetic and deterministic, but it is not yet a standalone
    decompositional certificate replay checker.

    The local checker soundness facts in `A002_08__Soundness` presently certify
    accepted-result shape. The stronger schema-inversion statements for K, S,
    and MP remain planned proof work.

    The total formula wrapper uses

      formula_bound c = S c.

    This is executable and bounded. Proving the full constructor theorem
    `is_formula_imp` for that wrapper requires either an A001 code-growth lemma
    or a revised formula-bound design with a locally provable fuel monotonicity
    argument.

    Compact IO views such as `A002_IO_Z` and `Verify_Diagnostic_Z` are provided
    so `vm_compute` examples can print binary integers rather than large Peano
    numerals.
